%%abcts a `-` INSIDE a grace group. `var inTie` is declared outside the group's own loop,
%%abcts `getCoreNote` puts `startTie` on the grace whose `-` it read, and the NEXT
%%abcts iteration takes `endTie` from it (`abc_parse_music.js:685-712`).
X:1
T:two graces tied
L:1/8
K:C
{a-a}C2 D2|

X:2
T:three graces, the middle one both ends
L:1/8
K:C
{a-a-a}C2 D2|

X:3
T:tied across two different pitches, which draws a SLUR
L:1/8
K:C
{a-b}C2 D2|

X:4
T:a startTie the group never closes
L:1/8
K:C
{a-}C2 {a}D2|

X:5
T:a tie inside a group that also carries a slur
L:1/8
K:C
{(a-a)}C2 D2|

X:6
T:tied graces on a chord
L:1/8
K:C
{a-a}[CEG]2 D2|

X:7
T:a tied pair beside an acciaccatura
L:1/8
K:C
{/a-a}C2 D2|

X:8
T:tied graces in a group long enough to beam
L:1/8
K:C
{aa-aa}C2 D2|
